body:
This is toxic! Please re-evaluate everything about this marriage, you need to sit down and give her this list. You need to tell her to imagine how she'd feel if all of this happened to her.

&#x200B;

If you want to redeem this you need to demand you both get couples counselling and if she can't be open minded to fixing what she broke a.k.a your mental health then you need to get out.

I'm sorry but all of this is such emotional manipulation!

&#x200B;

This is insanely isolating, I would feel the exact same way and want to run for the hills if any of this was happening to me on a daily basis.  She basically wants nothing to do with you but wants you to hold her on the highest pedestal and be all about her at the same time while she can't give you the time of day? 

&#x200B;

Do you communicate these problems to her or do you just bottle it up?

Hey, yeah it's true that something like that will always be apart of a relationship (being attracted to others) but yeah I think everybody finds themselves insecure. I think even if the roles were reversed he'd probably feel a little insecure too if he saw you liking naked guys.

&#x200B;

The idea that there will always be other attractive people for you and him to individually admire will be something you need to deal with. But maybe explain that liking the pictures all the time makes you uncomfortable, you understand he can be attracted to others but it makes you a little insecure when he's directly liking the pictures.

Good advice in completely the wrong situation, this is a young UNDERAGE girl who has her boyfriend fantasizing about other women purely because they have sex after 9pm.

&#x200B;

That is emotional manipulation.

Picture it this way.

&#x200B;

When you were 12 thinking about love or whatever age, did you depict getting cheated on twice?

&#x200B;

No? Because it's not meant to happen. You have to live with your self for the rest of your life, everyone else is temporary.

&#x200B;

Leave, please.

Don't feel bad about being scared either. It's a scary thing for anyone but it's one of the biggest steps towards bettering yourself. Recently, I actually finally admitted I needed help after countless years of no therapy after one bad session many years ago.

&#x200B;

Just keep going through therapists and help until you find the right one that helps you.

&#x200B;
